  "conformance_details": {
    "initialization": "Ranked maps k, max_score, empty selected, and ordered scores; HardExclusive maps seat/candidate bounds, max_score, null allocation, and per-seat scores; immutable and mutable Soft map weight_total, max_score, scores, and zero extra awards to their canonical Init states.",
    "step-simulation": "Variant-qualified executable actions map only to their matching ranked, hard-exclusive, immutable-soft, or mutable-soft canonical action; score writers map to the complete reset transition and rejected guards may stutter.",
    "observation-agreement": "All 17 profile-qualified correspondence fields project directly: ranked k/max_score/selected/scores, hard bounds/allocation/scores, and immutable/mutable soft weight_total/max_score/scores/extra.",
    "commit-agreement": "Each accepted rank selection, seat evaluation, or soft unit award is one selection-authority commit; score updates are provider-owned environment transitions with canonical reset frames.",
    "failure-persistence-agreement": "No crash, torn selection/reset, retry, staged concurrent winner, or recovery action is modeled.",
    "rely-discharge": "Deployment chooses one variant, supplies its finite bounds/enumeration, serializes all state, and ensures score writers perform the variant's complete reset.",
    "liveness-preservation": "No eventual fill, award completion, fairness, selection coverage, or latency guarantee is transferred for any variant.",
    "tcb-closure": "Every outcome or score writer is inventoried under its variant-qualified executable method; the shared Soft methods receive separate immutable and mutable action mappings, and no guarantee transfers across variants without a theorem."
  },
